@HD	VN:1.6	SO:unsorted	GO:query
@SQ	SN:chr1	LN:240
@SQ	SN:chr2	LN:240
@CO	07-circles-and-two-copy.
@CO	self_circle: self-ligated restriction fragment chr1:41-120 sheared at chr1:80/81: molecule chr1:81-120 | chr1:41-80, L=80, reads 50/50.
@CO	self_circle: R1 = chr1:81-120 (fwd) + supp chr1:41-50; R2 = chr1:41-80 (rev) + supp chr1:111-120. Overlap f[30,50) = chr1:111-120 + chr1:41-50. Primaries face outward and their intervals do not intersect.
@CO	sister_chromatid: one locus twice, chr2:41-80 | chr2:41-80, L=80, reads 60/60. R1 = chr2:41-80 + supp chr2:41-60; R2 = chr2:41-80 (rev) + supp chr2:61-80.
@CO	sister_chromatid: true overlap f[20,60) = copy1 chr2:61-80 (R1 primary vs R2 supp) + copy2 chr2:41-60 (R1 supp vs R2 primary). The PRIMARIES share chr2:41-80 on the reference but observe different molecule bases (decoy L=40).
@CO	two_copy_past_end: chr1:161-185 twice, L=50, R1 15 bp (copy 1), R2 30 bp = primary chr1:161-185 5S25M (rev, copy 2) + supplementary chr1:181-185 5M25H (rev, the last 5 bases of copy 1). The mates do not meet.
@CO	two_copy_indistinguishable: chr2:141-170 | chr2:151-190, L=70, R1 25 bp chr2:141-165, R2 30 bp chr2:161-190. The mates do not meet, but the alignments are identical to a 50 bp colinear fragment chr2:141-190.
